Explanation :

- Generics: Leaderboard<T> allows the leaderboard to work with different object types.
- Comparator: Defines the ranking order of teams.
- comparingInt(): Compares integer values such as points.
- reversed(): Arranges points and goal difference in descending order.
- thenComparing(): Applies the next condition when two teams have equal points or goal difference.
- Alphabetical ordering: Team names are compared when both numerical values are equal.
- Wildcard (List<? extends T>): Allows the constructor to accept a list containing objects of type T or its subclasses.

Time complexity :

Operation	Complexity
Adding teams	O(1) average
Sorting teams	O(n log n)
Displaying teams	O(n)
Copying input list	O(n)